WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.440
- Our next guest is a
very talented musician,

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.210
who's song "Kings &amp; Queens"

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:06.680
has been stuck in all our
heads for the last year.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.950
Her latest single is called
"My Head &amp; My Heart,"

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:11.470
and it's also on the
album, "Heaven &amp; Hell."

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:13.860
Clearly she enjoys a
good conjunction, y'all.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.097
Please welcome Ava Max, everybody.

00:00:16.097 --> 00:00:20.491
(audience clapping)
(bright upbeat music)

00:00:20.491 --> 00:00:21.491
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:23.981
You look incredible.

00:00:23.981 --> 00:00:26.971
(bright upbeat music continues)

00:00:26.971 --> 00:00:28.450
- Hello, again!
- Hi.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:29.510
- I know we can't hug.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:31.090
Hot air balloons are
like my favorite thing.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.700
- You know, I've never been on one, but-

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:33.850
- You haven't?
- I'm living through

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:34.740
my shirt right now.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.400
- I told my friends, okay, funny story,

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.260
I love going on them.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.330
But I told my friends, were
in like Scotland or Ireland,

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:40.370
I can't remember, I think Scotland.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:41.900
And they were like, "Okay,
we'll do it, we'll do it."

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.880
And they were afraid, and
literally landed so hard.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.180
Something happened and
it fell over. (laughs)

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:46.440
- Oh, my God, that's terrifying.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.037
- And I was like the one going,

00:00:48.037 --> 00:00:50.440
"You're gonna love it."
(audience laughing)

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.740
Anyway. Well, the last
time that I saw you,

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:53.970
we talked about how you got started.

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.810
But I didn't know your mama was a singer?

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:58.490
- Yes. She has a beautiful voice.

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:00.270
She can out-sing me any day.

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.750
She has an incredible
Operatic voice, you know?

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:04.890
She never fulfilled it fully her dream,

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.210
'cause she had kids, but...

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.500
And she was, you know, an
immigrant to the States,

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.470
and she got to work immediately,

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.350
'cause they didn't have money

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:13.900
when they came to the States,
and they didn't have jobs.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.160
So, you know, she dedicated
her life to her kids.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:17.810
- So, you were born in Wisconsin,

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.460
but so, where were your parents from?

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:20.560
- [Ava] Albania?

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:23.460
- I feel like there's a lot
of great singers from Albania.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.700
Like there's you, there's Rita Ora.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:28.290
There's Dua Lipa, there's Bebe Rexha.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:29.640
There's a lot of singers from...

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:30.709
What's happening there?

00:01:30.709 --> 00:01:32.310
What's happening?
- I don't know. (laughs)

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:34.010
I don't know, but my entire family,

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:35.570
grandma, grandpas, uncles-

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:37.207
- And you're all unbelievably ugly.

00:01:37.207 --> 00:01:38.470
That's yeah.
(Ava laughing)

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.720
You're also all very hard to look at,

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:41.553
so that's yeah.

00:01:41.553 --> 00:01:43.970
I mean, what's happening there?

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:44.980
What's, why?

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:46.530
- Very good makeup.
- It's the good water?

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:47.440
Like what's happening?

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.067
Like, is it a passionate?

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:51.040
- I think it's in our blood.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.277
It's very passionate.
- Okay.

00:01:52.277 --> 00:01:53.110
- We're very passionate.

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:54.080
We're kind of like,

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.900
you know, like we use their hands a lot.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.020
We're very like...

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:59.290
We kind of sing our
words in a way. (laughs)

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:02.460
Everyone tells me, "Oh, you
sing kind of when you talk."

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.780
And I'm just like, "I
don't know, but maybe I-"

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.277
- You just said, "I don't know, but."

00:02:06.277 --> 00:02:07.480
(audience laughing)

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:10.480
- Maybe I was always
meant to sing. (laughs)

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:11.670
- It's awesome though.

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:13.720
I didn't realize how many
people were from Albania.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:15.450
I was like, "Wow. All their relatives."

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:16.283
I thought that was interesting.

00:02:16.283 --> 00:02:17.161
- I love that.

00:02:17.161 --> 00:02:18.257
They're like basically my sisters.

00:02:18.257 --> 00:02:20.890
And I feel like they're
like my musical sisters.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:22.300
- Yeah. It's a good bunch.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.920
Y'all would be the most
amazing girl group ever.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:26.480
Well, do you remember the very first time

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:27.980
that you ever tried to write a song?

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.680
Cause you're a writer as
well, not just a singer?

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:31.090
- I do remember.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.210
There was a few instances.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:36.280
One, I wrote a song called
"Treat Me Like A Lady" at 13.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:38.190
- At 13.
- And what did I know about-

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:39.110
- You were getting puberty, yeah.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:40.420
- What did I know though?

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:43.850
So, I was way ahead of my female
empowerment game back then.

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:44.990
- Yes.
- Like I knew what

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:46.960
I was gonna write about
even way back then,

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:47.860
with that subconsciously.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:49.810
- You noticed something
was wrong early on?

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:51.910
- I didn't like the way women,

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:54.220
I was like looking how they were treated.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:55.990
And I wrote a song called
"Treat Me Like A Lady."

00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:56.823
Like who does that at 13?

00:02:56.823 --> 00:02:58.120
- I love that.
- Very strange.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.780
But, I don't really remember it.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.810
I just remember the title and
it being very like soulful.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.320
It was kinda like an R&amp;B song.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:06.560
- Yeah.
- And I just went in-

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.880
- My first songs were like that too.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.070
I think that was the '90s
influence really for me too.

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:11.940
Yes.
- The best.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.830
Yes. All the best R&amp;B, wow!

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.770
Well, your new single
is "My Head &amp; My Heart."

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:16.870
So, what were you going through?

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:19.210
Was that a relationship kind
of thing, or friendship or?

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:21.560
- You know, I'm always living my art.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:22.960
It's very strange.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:23.793
- Do you ever find that you're...

00:03:23.793 --> 00:03:25.980
Like you feel like you're
like fortune telling?

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:27.090
Like, you'll write a song,

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.950
and then it happens?
- And then it happens.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:29.783
Did that ever happen to you?

00:03:29.783 --> 00:03:30.616
'Cause that-

00:03:30.616 --> 00:03:31.990
- Yes.
- It's insanity.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:32.823
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:32.823 --> 00:03:34.208
- And I'm starting to-
- And did I project it?

00:03:34.208 --> 00:03:35.041
- Exactly, did I project-

00:03:35.041 --> 00:03:36.731
- I talk about these things in therapy.

00:03:36.731 --> 00:03:37.650
(audience laughing)

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.430
- I think I need to do. (laughs)

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:41.610
'Cause I put it out there,
and then it happens to me,

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:44.990
and then I'm like, "Oh, wow.
Life imitates art in a way."

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:47.210
And it makes sense 'cause
energy is everything.

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:49.010
What you put out there, you get back.

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:51.810
And so, yeah, all my songs
are kind of me right now.

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:53.620
I am a torn,

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:55.150
torn kind of part.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:56.390
I'm always like this or that.

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:57.223
Like, I'm always...

00:03:57.223 --> 00:04:00.510
I never know what I truly want
in relationships, you know?

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:01.701
And that's just who I am.

00:04:01.701 --> 00:04:02.710
- And I think that we don't...

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:04.300
Maybe you don't have to know that.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.570
Maybe it's like a process,
like that you learn,

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:08.220
and it's always gonna be
different with different people?

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.810
- Exactly. I feel like you'll
know when you know, right?

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.931
When it's...
- Well, I don't know.

00:04:12.931 --> 00:04:15.900
- Right? (laughs)
- I don't know,

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.010
anymore.
(audience laughing)

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:18.110
- Let's just say that.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:20.430
- Is it true that your mom,

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:22.200
you said she studied Opera, right?

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.270
Did you ever do any of
that kinda stuff with her?

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:25.693
Did she ever-
- You know, I never-

00:04:25.693 --> 00:04:27.380
- Sing in the house, where you're like,

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:28.540
let me sing with her?

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.330
- I always sang pop,
she always sang opera.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.960
So, it was chest, my voice and hers,

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.013
was like all head voice, and
I can never do what she did.

00:04:35.013 --> 00:04:36.450
- It's very Mariah Carey.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:37.960
I feel like her mom was an opera singer.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.160
- So weird, right?
- And then she did pop.

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:39.993
Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:04:39.993 --> 00:04:41.850
- Yeah. We also have the same birthmark.

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:43.090
I know that sounds crazy.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:44.030
- You do?
- I'm not-

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:46.170
- The fact that you know that,
doesn't sound weird at all.

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:48.260
- (laughs) It's I love Mariah Carey.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:49.830
I love Mariah Carey.
- I do too. I do too.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:50.900
- My number one.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:52.930
And so, I remember seeing a picture.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:54.550
I think the "Butterfly"
record is on the end.

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:55.383
She was like...

00:04:55.383 --> 00:04:56.800
She was pretty much like just a bra,

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.199
like pretty much naked.
- Yeah.

00:04:58.199 --> 00:04:59.032
- And I used to-
- It was like Tan.

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:01.150
It looks like everything was
there like brown and beige.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:03.220
- I have birth mark right
underneath my belly button,

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:04.347
same one.
- Wow!

00:05:04.347 --> 00:05:06.080
- And our mothers are Opera singers.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:07.560
Mariah, did we?
- I didn't know

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:09.430
she was there like ultimate.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:10.420
She's very nice.

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:11.253
- I love-

00:05:11.253 --> 00:05:12.620
- I've run into her a few
times, she was so nice.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:14.220
- In a way, her songs
taught me how to sing.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:15.710
I would be in my basement
singing her songs

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.910
over, and over, and over.
- She's one of mine as well.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:18.743
Yeah.
- The best.

00:05:18.743 --> 00:05:21.940
- And especially just her
octaves, like are insane.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:23.210
- Yes.
- It's like, "Shut up!"

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:25.207
- I'm like, "Why you so good?"
- So talented, yeah.

00:05:25.207 --> 00:05:26.350
(audience laughing)

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:29.010
Well, Ava's single is
called "My Head &amp; My Heart."

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.830
It's on her Heaven &amp; Hell" album.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.417
Check it out, everybody, you're
gonna wanna check it out.

